{
  "version": "6",
  "_comment": [
    "Controlled vocabulary for inferring meaning from path segments when a file",
    "has no MOLNG/flowcell match in metadata.csv.",
    "",
    "Seeded from the vocabulary actually present in the CSV's Scientific Projects,",
    "Analysis Goals, and Project Type columns. Edit freely -- build_index.py reads",
    "this at runtime and stamps vocab_version onto every inferred association, so",
    "the knowledge store records which dictionary produced a given claim.",
    "",
    "Matching is case-insensitive against tokens split out of each path segment.",
    "Anything in 'ambiguous' is refused even if it matches, per the rule that a",
    "too-vague token should not be interpreted at all.",
    "",
    "v6 (2026-09-04, from the H19 stroke discovery run): the lab writes the",
    "photothrombotic stroke model as 'pt', never as 'stroke'. A search on 'stroke'",
    "returned 39 paths; the actual imaging cohort is ~1,740 files and 375 GB named",
    "with 'pt'. But bare 'pt' is only ~40% correct on this collection -- it also",
    "means PT_Rabies (1,630), EndNote 'Pt 15' page ranges (1,194) and PT_Model",
    "deep-learning checkpoints (112). So 'pt' is REFUSED in 'ambiguous', and the",
    "model is captured through bigrams (pt_h19, lesion_pt, pt_24h ...) that the",
    "tokenizer's adjacent-pair pass already produces. Same reasoning refuses",
    "'peri' (all 17 hits are a person's name, not peri-infarct),",
    "'nc' (negative control vs neural crest) and '7d' (a plasmid file, not 7 days).",
    "Neurovascular markers were absent entirely and are now in 'gene'.",
    "",
    "Known residue in v6: 'pt7' also matches journal citations written '(Pt 7)'",
    "-- 4 reference PDFs in an EndNote library folder are tagged photothrombotic.",
    "Kept anyway: 174 correct vs 4 wrong, and the 4 are non-data reference PDFs.",
    "Measured precision of the photothrombotic terms overall is 1050/1054."
  ],
